.TH STOP-MU2EDAQ-COMMANDLINE-TOOLS.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh \- signal the pidfile PID and clean up
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-keep\-logs ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the pidfile exists and its PID answers
.BR "kill \-0" ,
sends SIGTERM, polls once a second for up to
.I SECS
seconds, and sends SIGKILL if the process is still alive.
It does not check that the PID belongs to
.BR mu2edaq\-tools .
A PID that is not running is reported as stale.
The pidfile is then removed.
.PP
It then deletes every
.I __pycache__
directory under the checkout (including
.IR venv/ )
and, unless
.B \-\-keep\-logs
is given, runs
.B rm \-rf
on the log directory.
.PP
No tool in this package writes logs or a log directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Seconds between SIGTERM and SIGKILL.
Default 10.
A non-integer value makes the wait loop's test fail at once, so SIGKILL
follows immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-logs
Do not delete the log directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the script's header comment and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_PIDFILE
Pidfile location.
Default:
.I .mu2edaq\-tools.pid
in the checkout.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_LOG_DIR
Directory to delete.
Default:
.I logs
in the checkout.
This is also the environment override for the
.B log_dir
setting of
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1);
whatever directory it names is removed recursively, without confirmation.
A relative value is resolved against the current directory.
The
.B log_dir
key in the config file is not consulted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including when there was nothing to stop.
.TP
.B 1
.B \-\-timeout
without an argument.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option.
.SH BUGS
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1)
never removes its pidfile, so after any completed run the file holds a PID
that may since have been reused by an unrelated process of the same user,
which this script will then terminate.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
\&./stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh \-\-keep\-logs
\&./stop\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh \-\-timeout 30
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
